# RUN 5 -- 19 September 2026.  The weld to the grazing bound is now part of the
# PUBLIC path, not a separate audit script: weld() certifies the bridge cell
# [rquarter, rquarter+1e-10] like any other cell and encloses
# V(rquarter+1e-10) - V(r0)/4, requiring the enclosure to be strictly positive.
# That places the bridge's upper end above the TRUE quarter radius -- rquarter
# itself comes from brentq in binary64 -- so the certified window and the
# elementary bound overlap and the interval is covered with no gap.  A failure of
# either half now sets the exit code.  The runner also reports WELD GAP if the
# window cap min(rquarter, r0-0.1) ever bites, which on this grid it does not
# (largest rquarter 7.063 against r0-0.1 = 11.9).
#
# The (nc, S, M) counts are IDENTICAL to runs 1-4 in all six configurations.
#
# Underpinning both: V is strictly increasing on r >= 2M for every E > 1, which
# is what makes cap_full.r_of_V's two-sided test an enclosure of the preimage
# rather than of one branch.  With r = 2M+s, V' = 2rN/D_E^2 and
#     N(2M+s) = b s^2 + 3M(b+1) s + 2M^2(b+1),   b = E^2-1,
# all coefficients positive, constant term 2M^2(b+1) > 0.  Verified symbolically
# for general M; recorded in the manuscript as qualification (iv).
E  r0  bb  rquarter  RESULT  nc S M  time
E=1.2 r0=8 bb=0.440 rquarter=4.958 : PASS (nc=374 S=66 M=35 354s)
  weld [4.958199488,4.958199488] tag=S ; V(upper)-V(r0)/4 in [1.1064160032e-9, 1.1064160032e-9] > 0 ? True : OK
E=1.6 r0=8 bb=1.560 rquarter=4.759 : PASS (nc=399 S=65 M=43 366s)
  weld [4.758838390,4.758838390] tag=S ; V(upper)-V(r0)/4 in [4.0919494657e-10, 4.0919494657e-10] > 0 ? True : OK
E=2.5 r0=8 bb=5.250 rquarter=4.659 : PASS (nc=427 S=69 M=46 397s)
  weld [4.659381426,4.659381426] tag=S ; V(upper)-V(r0)/4 in [1.32262860623e-10, 1.32262860623e-10] > 0 ? True : OK
E=1.2 r0=12 bb=0.440 rquarter=7.063 : PASS (nc=917 S=140 M=75 948s)
  weld [7.063069237,7.063069237] tag=S ; V(upper)-V(r0)/4 in [1.95094972829e-9, 1.95094972829e-9] > 0 ? True : OK
E=1.6 r0=12 bb=1.560 rquarter=6.765 : PASS (nc=939 S=148 M=73 959s)
  weld [6.765456692,6.765456692] tag=S ; V(upper)-V(r0)/4 in [6.62314499293e-10, 6.62314499293e-10] > 0 ? True : OK
E=2.5 r0=12 bb=5.250 rquarter=6.634 : PASS (nc=964 S=150 M=75 998s)
  weld [6.634406869,6.634406869] tag=S ; V(upper)-V(r0)/4 in [2.08160878512e-10, 2.08160878512e-10] > 0 ? True : OK
