# Validated interval-arithmetic certificates for the single-crossing property
# (B), over a grid of (E, r0).  Produced by no_inversion_schwarzschild_CAP_grid.py.
# RUN 4 -- 18 September 2026, after two counter fixes in the grid runner.
# (i) cert() returns 'S' or 'M', both truthy, so the wide-cell branch counted
#     every success as 'S': the S/M split could be wrong, though the certified
#     disjunction and hence PASS/FAIL could not.
# (ii) the runner printed FAIL without propagating a nonzero exit code, which
#     misleads any automation reading only the exit status.  It now exits 1.
# The counts below are IDENTICAL to runs 1-3 in all six configurations, which
# says the first bug never fired on these grids: no wide cell ever certified by
# the PP<0 branch here.  The defect was real in the code and latent in the runs,
# and the archived counts of the earlier runs therefore stand.
